      "body": "## Context\n\n`findDirtyRepos()` in `cmd/gitops/init.go` scans `extensions/` and `skins/` for git repos with uncommitted changes. It returns a list of dirty repo paths. It has no unit test coverage.\n\n## What to test\n\nAdd table-driven tests in `cmd/gitops/init_test.go` covering:\n\n1. **Clean repo not reported** — create a git repo with all changes committed. Verify it is not in the returned list.\n2. **Dirty repo reported** — create a git repo with uncommitted changes. Verify it appears in the returned list.\n3. **Gitlink file skipped** — create a subdirectory with a `.git` file (not directory). Verify it is not reported.\n4. **Non-git directory skipped** — create a subdirectory without `.git`. Verify it is not reported.\n5. **Empty extensions/skins** — verify empty list returned when directories are empty.\n6. **Missing directories** — verify empty list returned when `extensions/` and `skins/` don't exist.\n\n## Hints\n\n- Use `t.TempDir()` for test directories\n- Create the `extensions/` subdirectory structure inside the temp dir\n- Use `exec.Command` to run git init, git add, git commit in the temp repos\n- The function signature is `findDirtyRepos(installPath string) []string`\n\nPart of #241",
